2) Approach proposal:
- Question: distributional similarity between forward-model sampled trajectories and ground-truth MD across backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, top TICA components.

Design elements to propose:
- Data/representations: compute per-residue backbone dihedrals (φ, ψ) per frame; sidechain χ angles per rotatable bond; TICA on some featurization (e.g., pairwise distances between heavy atoms, or sine/cosine of torsions) — TICA defined by MD trajectory (reference), then project both MD and forward trajectories onto the same TICA basis.
- Metric of distributional similarity: 
  - KLD / Jensen–Shannon divergence, Earth Mover's Distance (Wasserstein-1), Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD), cosine of mean embedding, Bhattacharyya distance, overlap coefficient.
  - Need to handle periodic angular data for torsions: wrap angles, use circular statistics / von Mises KLD, or embed as (sin, cos) pairs rather than raw angles.
- Statistical tests: 
  - Two-sample tests: KS test (on unwrapped or on sin/cos coordinates), Anderson-Darling, energy distance, MMD with permutation test for significance; for high-dim TICA component distributions use multivariate two-sample tests (energy distance, FREED/Wasserstein bootstrap), or compare marginal distributions per component (cheaper, more interpretable).
  - Effect-size reporting: rather than p-values alone, report similarity scores and calibrated thresholds.
- Replicates/trajectories: generate N_fwd independent forward trajectories and N_MD reference trajectories (if available); pool frames but account for autocorrelation — subsample/block along time; use bootstrap over trajectories to get confidence intervals on the similarity metric.
- Re-referencing/alignment: 
  - TICA: fit eigendecomposition on the MD reference trajectories (or pooled MD), apply to forward trajectories with the same transformation (no refit per trajectory) — that's the "aligned" basis making distributions comparable.
  - Alignment for TICA sign ambiguity: TICA components have sign ambiguity; ensure sign convention fixed between fitting and projecting (and possibly flip for consistency across replicates).
  - Optionally remove overall rotational/translational motion before computing internal coordinates (rmsd-fit to a reference frame or use internal coords which are automatically rot-trans invariant).
- Cross-validation: to avoid overfitting similarity to the same MD data used for TICA fitting, do a split: fit TICA on MD train set, evaluate distributional similarity on held-out MD test set vs forward samples. This is a key design choice.
- Baselines/controls: 
